# ZL Loudness Makeup for WebCLAP

ZLLMakeup by ZL Audio (zsliu98), a loudness make-up plugin, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official ZL Audio
release.

- ZLLMakeup: https://github.com/ZL-Audio/ZLLMakeup (commit cd21094, version 0.2.5)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-zl-lmakeup.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

Changes in this port (`patches/zl-lmakeup-webclap.patch`): the processor builds without its editor, and a block
without a transport has no position. The Aux (sidechain) input, the reference Effect mode makes the input's
loudness up to, is a second input port; when the host feeds it nothing it is silent and Effect mode turns the input
down as far as Bound allows. The editor's UI settings (style, window size) live in the page's memory and are gone
when it reloads.

